WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.340
If our time with the SCP Foundation has taught
us anything, it’s that books are evil and

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.820
not to be trusted.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:10.620
This is why, right now, you’re doing the
right thing and watching some nice, wholesome

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:16.439
YouTube videos rather than potentially exposing
your delicate mind to the devilry of the written

00:00:16.439 --> 00:00:17.439
word.

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:18.630
Think we’re overexaggerating here?

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.630
Ha!

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:20.990
That’s how they get you!

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.109
Sure, you could pick up a book right now and
give it a read, but what if it was SCP-592,

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:27.890
the Inaccurate History Book?

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.730
Where just reading beyond a certain point
will drive you mad, and start to inflict potentially

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.690
deadly wounds caused by a nightmarish, retroactively
altered past.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.230
Or what if you decided you wanted to read
some slightly more niche historical subjects,

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:46.550
and picked up a vintage copy of A Chronicle
of the Daevas, not knowing this is also An

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.620
Incomplete Chronicle, classified as SCP-140.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.920
You get a paper cut on one of those aging,
yellow pages, and boom!

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.250
You’re suddenly forced into slavery in a
Daevite labor camp.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.730
Maybe that rightly scared you off of history.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:06.130
You want to do something a little more scientific,
so you grab a copy of SCP-1025, the Encyclopedia

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.860
of Common Diseases.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.070
Next thing you know, agents of the CDC are
surrounding you, wearing hazmat suits and

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:17.470
setting up a secure quarantine tent because
they think you have a rare strain of Super-Mega-Ebola.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.500
Not even some nice, escapist fantasy is safe.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.439
You pick up a copy of SCP-1230, a Hero Is
Born, to have a magical fantasy adventure

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:26.650
in your dreams.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.120
But then when you wake up, you’ve lost all
your lust for life because it just can’t

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.549
measure up to the fantasy.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:38.990
And don’t even get us started on SCP-3512,
an anomalous book of pick-up artist tips called

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.690
“The More You Know: A Pick-Up Artist’s
Guide.”

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:46.340
Sure, it may have a forward by Snoop Dogg
himself, and it may be less dangerous to read

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.680
than the other books here, but considering
it’s ultimately a book of Fifthist rituals

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:55.509
designed to help you mind-control women for
romantic purposes, you’re probably a horrible

00:01:55.509 --> 00:01:57.399
person if you want a copy.

00:01:57.399 --> 00:02:01.000
So we’re all on the same page now: Books
are evil.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.700
They’re best avoided at all costs.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.229
And what is a catalog or magazine but a very
thin book, right?

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:10.250
So they’re Evil-Lite.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.250
You cannot trust them under any circumstances.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.200
That’s why, when Professor Snider got a
strange new magazine delivered directly into

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.220
his mailbox, it didn’t take long for him
to smell a rat and take it down to his local

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.310
SCP Foundation containment site for some preliminary
tests.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.750
The magazine’s cover read, “The Official
SCP Sales Catalog.”

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.000
Already, this was weird enough.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.240
The SCP Foundation doesn’t produce any kind
of sales catalog - that’s more Marshall,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.580
Carter, and Dark’s modus operandi.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:45.831
But this catalog had Dr. Jack Bright on the
cover, smiling and holding SCP-066 - The living

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:50.130
ball of yarn known as Eric’s Toy - like
he was overjoyed with it.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.780
When Professor Snider showed the cover to
Dr. Bright himself, he said that it must just

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:57.800
be some high-quality photoshop, because he
never took a photo like that.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:03.350
The cover also bore slogans like “Our best
issue ever!” and “Hundreds of bargains!”,

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:08.440
and Professor Snider soon found that both
of these bizarre slogans were true, in a manner

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.470
of speaking.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:14.960
The inside of the catalog contained comprehensive
records of almost every SCP recorded on the

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.260
database, complete with photos and descriptions.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:23.470
Though rather than the sterile scientific
depictions typical of an SCP Foundation document,

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.650
these descriptions were written like peppy
sales copy, aimed at selling off the “products”

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.650
in question.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:33.620
Mortified by the potential security breach
he was holding, Professor Snider decided to

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.750
take a look through the catalog and assess
the damage, flicking between pages, both dazzled

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.450
and terrified by just how deep this thing
went…

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:47.840
ITEM #063 - “The World’s Greatest TothBrush”
Don’t let the typo fool you: this toothbrush

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.530
is out of this world!

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:54.290
No toothpaste needed, just gently scrub your
teeth and, like magic, all that nasty plaque

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.160
is completely obliterated!

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.300
And for those ground-in countertop stains,
look no further than The World’s Greatest

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.700
TothBrush!

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.180
Available in blue, pink, and green.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:09.300
SCP-063, of course, being a toothbrush capable
of completely expunging matter from existence

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.370
with its anomalous bristles.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:16.621
ITEM #123 - “Contained Miniature Black Hole”
Back in stock after so many requests, this

00:04:16.621 --> 00:04:20.620
black hole is guaranteed to spaghettify anything
you throw at it.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.840
Great for science projects and parties!

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.340
And what better way to say “I love you”
than with the gift of a contained miniature

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.560
black hole?

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.450
Order now while supplies last!

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.900
Warning: contains small parts.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:35.510
It goes without saying why ever giving the
public access to a dangerous and unstable

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:40.110
contained black hole would be a disaster of
a truly cosmic magnitude.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.630
ITEM#244 - “Ice Fog Jar”
Why waste electric-bill money on expensive

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.950
refrigerators?

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:50.510
This jar will turn an enclosed space of any
size into your own private meat-locker!

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:54.470
Freeze whatever you want: just pop off the
lid and watch it go!

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.080
Oh boy.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.160
Engaging with SCP-244 is an extremely risky
business.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.190
Once the fog from the jar has reduced the
ambient temperature of the room significantly,

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:10.330
it runs the risk of bringing in SCP-244-2,
a deadly gaseous entity that can kill people

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.010
with an instant flash-freezing effect.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.500
ITEM #340 – “Insanity Candy”
A truly maddening prank!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:21.530
Trick your friends into eating these covert
candies and watch them literally go out of

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.030
their minds!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.470
Available in 5-packs.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.960
Professor Snider winced at the memories this
one brought on.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:33.910
SCP-340, now a kind of deadly virus, had once
been a particularly lethal packet of M&amp;Ms

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:38.350
capable of inducing various types of severe
mental illness in its victims.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.790
This was no prank, unless you happened to
be an extreme sadist with no regard for human

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:47.640
life and happiness - Like all the prank channels
that have since been wiped from YouTube.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.950
ITEM #447 - “Ball of Green Slime”
What can you do with it?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.590
What CAN’T you do with it?

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:58.520
Use it as a lubricant, top off your gas tank,
style your hair, or even dress up your salads

00:05:58.520 --> 00:05:59.650
and sundaes!

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.570
The possibilities are endless!

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.490
Now available in blue.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:06.380
WARNING: Do not apply to dead bodies.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.250
Professor Snider gulped and shuddered.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.780
The less said about that, the better.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.220
ITEM #500- "Panacea"
Got Ebola?

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.220
HIV?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.220
Cancer?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.220
Athlete's Foot?

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:17.220
This pill cures 'em all!

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.980
No malady is too incurable.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.020
OUT OF STOCK.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.240
This one was equal parts relieving and surprising.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:27.150
Relieving because at least this particularly
rare and powerful item was out of stock, and

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.760
when it was in stock, demanded a six-figure
payment per pill.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:35.139
Surprised by the fact anyone outside the Foundation
knew about the Panacea and wasn’t bashing

00:06:35.139 --> 00:06:37.260
down their doors to get it.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:41.930
ITEM #551- “Impossible Puzzle”
Throw out your Rubik’s Cube and put down

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:42.930
that crossword!

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.480
This is the puzzle to end all puzzles!

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.030
No-one in history has ever completed it, can
YOU?

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.230
Hours of fun!

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.271
This mind-shattering jigsaw puzzle was an
incredibly dangerous thing to market as a

00:06:54.271 --> 00:06:59.070
mere toy, especially considering some of its
victims lost their minds while attempting

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.190
to solve it.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:05.520
But Professor Snider could only brace himself,
turning page after page, because things were

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.500
about to get a whole lot worse in the Official
SCP Sales Catalog.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.040
ITEM#173 - “The Sculpture”
Spice up your living room with this unique

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.210
decoration!

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:20.890
The ultimate conversation piece that you will
literally never want to stop looking at!

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:24.340
Will draw the eye of all of your most distinguished
guests!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:29.580
ITEM#035 - “The Possessive Mask”
For those with a theatrical spirit, this mask

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:34.370
is a perfect way to hide that ugly mug while
also putting some fascinating new ideas in

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.400
your head!

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.810
This mask really speaks to you, and you’ll
find that after wearing it for a while, you’ll

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.050
lose a lot of weight, too!

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.020
ITEM#1981 - “Ronald Reagan Cut Up While
Talking”

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:49.020
Are you a big fan of analog horror and are
one of the few people who still own a working

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.020
VCR?

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.490
Do you have a real disdain for the late ex-President
Ronald Reagan?

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.210
Then you’ll love this classic taping of
one of his iconic speeches.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.670
No spoilers!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:02.900
ITEM#5000 - “The Suit”
Are you looking for the latest word in anomalous

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:06.120
fashion that can be ostentatious or very,
very discrete?

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.390
You’ll love this total exclusion suit - It’ll
do everything you need and more, especially

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:14.300
when it feels like the world is going crazy
around you!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.400
ITEM#055 - “The Anti-Meme”
It isn’t a sphere…

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.400
Uhhhhhhhhhhhh.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.800
I’m sorry, what were we trying to sell you
here again?

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.820
ITEM#2000 - “Deus Ex Machina”
For when you or the entire world just needs

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.270
