00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:13.760
And they’re completely harmless unless you
step on them!

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:18.260
ITEM#137 - “A Real Toy”
If you are a toy collector or a kid who doesn’t

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:23.350
have many friends, then A Real Toy will enhance
any and every playing experience!

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:26.100
See your games come to life like never before.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.670
Nothing beats playing with A Real Toy!

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:33.240
ITEM#272 - “An Old Iron Nail”
Want to keep something in place with zero

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.330
risk of escape?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.600
As long as it has a shadow, then the Old Iron
Nail has got you covered.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:43.080
Even has an in-built security system to keep
itself safe from any attempts to damage it!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:47.310
ITEM#4158 - “Big Charlie”
If you love to grill, then you’ll love Big

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:48.420
Charlie!

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:51.910
This mighty steer will keep you swimming in
steaks forever.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:56.560
Perfect for hosting barbecues for literally
everyone you know and everyone they know!

00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:01.060
ITEM#3108 - “The Nerfing Gun”
Are other people’s things nicer than yours?

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.550
That ain’t right!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:06.430
Get your hands on the Nerfing gun and knock
those jerks down a peg for good!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:09.200
Professor Snider couldn’t believe what he
was reading.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:14.040
This was textbook anomalous insanity; it even
had hard-cover copies of all the books we

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.149
were complaining about during the intro.

00:14:16.149 --> 00:14:20.390
It didn’t take long for the Official SCP
Sales Catalog to be designated an anomaly

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:26.519
itself, with the number SCP-000-J. But if
you can believe it, the madness didn’t even

00:14:26.519 --> 00:14:27.519
stop there.

00:14:27.519 --> 00:14:31.660
You see, the catalog didn’t just contain
the anomalies themselves as available products,

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:37.769
it also contained a wide variety of SCP Foundation
merchandise: t-shirts, books, DVDs, even video

00:14:37.769 --> 00:14:41.370
games and action figures, and so much more.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:46.470
Naturally, none of this had ever been authorized
by the SCP Foundation itself, or the staff

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:48.270
or anomalies in question.

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:52.399
To give you an idea of just how absurd this
gets, here are some examples of the fresh

00:14:52.399 --> 00:14:55.660
SCP Foundation merch inside the sales catalog.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:15:01.640
There was a white cotton t-shirt with a slogan
on it reading “I Survived The Wrath of SCP-682”,

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.910
along with a picture of SCP-682 on the shirt
itself.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:09.720
Available in size S-XXXL.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:16.560
A 30.48cm, or 12 inch, SCP-076-2 action figure,
with interchangeable wardrobe, accessories,

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.530
and carrying case shaped like SCP-076-1.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:24.580
When the real Able was shown a picture of
this action figure, he responded to it with

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:27.050
disgust, claiming it was an insult.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.970
Though to be fair, Able does think that about
a lot of things.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:33.850
A 2-disc CD titled “Dr. Clef’s Holiday
Hits”.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:37.839
Cover depicts Dr. Alto Clef in a Santa outfit
and holding a microphone.

00:15:37.839 --> 00:15:41.649
When he was questioned about it, Dr. Clef
denied ever recording such an album - He had

00:15:41.649 --> 00:15:46.640
only ever recorded a brief ukulele LP with
no vocals back in 1991.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:51.640
There was also a somewhat tasteless women’s
pinup calendar called “The Girls of SCP”,

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:55.130
featuring-- You know what, no, this one is
just creepy.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.130
Moving on.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:16:01.880
There was a 3-disc DVD set entitled 'SCP Brawl:
The Greatest SCP vs. SCP Fights'.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:07.240
The cover depicts SCPs 076-2, 173, and 682.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:11.850
Each disc is 9 hours long and features various
Keter level SCPs fighting each other.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:15.701
We’ve actually been releasing segments of
it on this channel for months now, and we

00:16:15.701 --> 00:16:18.970
intend to keep doing it, no matter how many
cease and desist letters we keep getting from

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.490
the Official SCP Sales Catalog.

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:24.490
There was also the two-disc soundtrack for
“FERNAND!

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:30.070
The Musical!”, a musical about the life
of SCP-082, which seems to contain some tracks

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:33.090
with the vocals of SCP-082 himself.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:37.959
When asked about this, SCP-082 spoke with
great pride about his time in musical theater,

00:16:37.959 --> 00:16:42.410
but given that he’s a pathological liar,
it’s difficult to know whether this is true.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:47.110
He’s the current owner of the album because
he ate the last owner and refuses to give

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:48.110
it back.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.320
Oh, and there was also an adorable, high-quality
SCP-999 plushie.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:56.790
Incidentally, this is the only one of these
products you can get in real life, from www.scpswag.com.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:02.440
No, we’re not kidding, check out the link
in the description after the video.

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:07.109
This whole anomaly ended up being a deeply
bizarre mystery for members of SCP Foundation

00:17:07.109 --> 00:17:08.289
personnel to investigate.

00:17:08.289 --> 00:17:13.019
While you could, theoretically, order multiple
iterations of each item, you would only get

00:17:13.019 --> 00:17:16.089
the one real one, surrounded by a number of
cheap copies.

00:17:16.089 --> 00:17:20.260
When Professor Snider called the helpline
directly, he was repeatedly rebuffed, with

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:24.819
the call operator hanging up on him if he
tried to do anything other than order an item.

00:17:24.819 --> 00:17:28.990
If you do order an item, it will simply end
up on your doorstep, and then the Foundation

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.399
will need to come and recontain it.

00:17:31.399 --> 00:17:36.179
Personnel wishing to test this item are required
to do so using their personal funds, as it’s

00:17:36.179 --> 00:17:38.919
essentially just throwing Foundation money
into a furnace.

00:17:38.919 --> 00:17:43.500
There currently only seems to be one of these
catalogs, but if ever one appears elsewhere,

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.830
it’s likely to give the SCP Foundation a
major headache.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.830
See?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.039
What did we tell you?

00:17:49.039 --> 00:17:51.610
Books, you just can’t trust them.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:53.070
Do you want our advice?

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:54.809
Just stick to YouTube videos.

00:17:54.809 --> 00:17:55.899
In fact…

00:17:55.899 --> 00:18:01.330
You should go check out “Why Everyone Wants
to Eat this Corpse - SCP-1176” and “SCP-049

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:07.159
- Boiled, Scrambled and Fried - Plague Doctor
Tale” for more bizarre and hilarious journeys

00:18:07.159 --> 00:18:08.710
into SCP Foundation lore!

